WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:05.070
Game of Thrones Season 7 Episode 4 begins
with the Lannisters taking gold and grain

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:06.450
from the reach.

00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:10.290
Most of this gold is going to the Iron Bank,
but Bronn also gets a cut.

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:11.290
He’s a mercenary.

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:15.259
He fought for Tyrion for gold, he fought at
the Blackwater for a knighthood.

00:00:15.259 --> 00:00:18.250
And Cersei gives him a noble bride as a bribe.

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:20.270
In the books, he’s still there at Stokeworth.

00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:25.680
He adopts Lollys’ son and names him Tyrion
just to mess with everyone . He murders his

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:27.990
wife’s brother-in-law for plotting against
him.

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:30.110
Basically, book-Bronn lives the good life.

00:00:30.110 --> 00:00:33.870
But in the show, Jaime keeps dragging Bronn
back to battle, and he doesn’t get much

00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:36.660
of a chance to spend all his gold.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:41.210
The Tarlys are taking food from the reach
for Cersei . So what will the people of the

00:00:41.210 --> 00:00:42.839
reach eat this winter?

00:00:42.839 --> 00:00:47.270
We saw last episode that Winterfell faces
a food shortage, so Sansa takes grain from

00:00:47.270 --> 00:00:51.769
the north . It looks like Westeros may run
out of food, and this is a problem in the

00:00:51.769 --> 00:00:52.769
books, too.

00:00:52.769 --> 00:00:57.309
“When winter comes, the realm will starve”
, Tyrion says, and some people use this to

00:00:57.309 --> 00:00:58.789
their advantage.

00:00:58.789 --> 00:01:03.079
Littlefinger hoards grain in the Vale, so
he can sell it at a high price when people

00:01:03.079 --> 00:01:07.530
are starving . The politics and economics
of food is important, and it’s cool to see

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:09.640
it acknowledged in the show.

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:13.829
Bronn questions Jaime over whether Cersei
could ever be a peaceful ruler , just like

00:01:13.829 --> 00:01:18.780
Olenna did last episode . And both times,
Jaime struggles to defend his sister.

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:22.560
To Olenna he argued that the ends justify
the means, it doesn’t matter if Cersei does

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:25.600
terrible things as long as it wins the war.

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:30.100
This episode he basically says hashtag Only
God Can Judge Me, except not even that, cause

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:34.470
Cersei killed the Pope . Jaime’s justifications
are getting weaker, and he’s eventually

00:01:34.470 --> 00:01:40.320
gotta admit that even though he loves Cersei,
she is awful and needs to be stopped.

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:45.630
At the capital, Cersei chats with Tycho, who
represents the Iron Bank.

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:48.420
He flatters her by comparing her to her father
Tywin.

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:52.869
Cersei’s daddy issues are a big part of
her hunger for power and pride.

00:01:52.869 --> 00:01:57.719
She always wanted Tywin’s approval, to be
like him, to rule like him . She even dresses

00:01:57.719 --> 00:01:58.719
like him.

00:01:58.719 --> 00:02:03.679
And her brutality is largely learned from
him . Go watch the Cersei video.

00:02:03.679 --> 00:02:09.289
And so Cersei’s goal is to control all of
Westeros . Which is going to cost money – Tycho

00:02:09.289 --> 00:02:11.060
offers to lend her more.

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:15.959
It is a bit weird to lend her more money at
the same time she’s paying back money – like

00:02:15.959 --> 00:02:18.170
couldn’t Cersei just hang on to this gold
she has?

00:02:18.170 --> 00:02:21.670
But whatever, the point is that the Bank’s
supporting Cersei.

00:02:21.670 --> 00:02:26.180
Cersei mentions she’s thinking of hiring
the Golden Company, an eastern sellsword group

00:02:26.180 --> 00:02:27.950
with a rich history in the books.

00:02:27.950 --> 00:02:32.870
They were originally founded by a Targaryen
bastard called Bittersteel , and still carry

00:02:32.870 --> 00:02:35.870
his gilded skull into battle.

00:02:35.870 --> 00:02:41.150
In Book 5, the Company invades Westeros as
part of Varys’ complex conspiracy – go

00:02:41.150 --> 00:02:43.220
watch the Varys video.

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:48.010
The point for the show is probably just that
Cersei is buying more soldiers.

00:02:48.010 --> 00:02:50.590
Up at Winterfell, Littlefinger talks with
Bran.

00:02:50.590 --> 00:02:55.290
As the eldest living Stark, Bran should technically
be Lord of Winterfell, so Petyr wants to get

00:02:55.290 --> 00:02:56.670
on his good side.

00:02:56.670 --> 00:03:00.970
He talks of his loyalty to Bran’s mother
Cat, who he loved since childhood, and he

00:03:00.970 --> 00:03:05.930
gives Bran a gift – the Valyrian steel dagger
that was used by an assassin to try to kill

00:03:05.930 --> 00:03:07.950
Bran in Season 1.

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:11.549
In the books, we’re told it was Joffrey
who ordered this attempt on Bran’s life

00:03:11.549 --> 00:03:14.450
, but the mystery’s never solved in the
show.

00:03:14.450 --> 00:03:19.980
Maybe in the show they’ll say it was Littlefinger
. Cause this dagger was a big part of Littlefinger’s

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:21.010
master plan.

00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:26.459
Petyr lied and told Catelyn this was Tyrion’s
dagger, so Cat abducted Tyrion, which led

00:03:26.459 --> 00:03:29.370
to war, which led to Petyr advancing politically.

00:03:29.370 --> 00:03:34.629
As Petyr says, “Chaos is a ladder” – he
used conflict to gain power.

00:03:34.629 --> 00:03:39.490
And now Bran repeats this line, showing that
he has seen some of what Petyr’s done.

00:03:39.490 --> 00:03:43.950
If the Starks find out that Petyr betrayed
Ned and lied to his dear Cat and started the

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:48.099
war that broke their family – Littlefinger
is totally screwed.

00:03:48.099 --> 00:03:50.140
Bran then speaks with Meera Reed.

00:03:50.140 --> 00:03:54.550
Meera spent three seasons fighting to protect
Bran, hunting and cooking for Bran, probably

00:03:54.550 --> 00:03:58.530
wiping Bran’s ass cause he’s paralysed,
all because Meera’s brother Jojen believed

00:03:58.530 --> 00:04:00.450
Bran needed to meet the raven.

00:04:00.450 --> 00:04:01.969
Now, Jojen’s dead.

00:04:01.969 --> 00:04:06.750
Hodor’s dead, Summer’s dead, the raven’s
dead, the children are dead, and in a way,

00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:08.290
Bran is dead.

00:04:08.290 --> 00:04:12.129
Now that he’s got all this psychic knowledge,
with everyone’s memories and experiences,

00:04:12.129 --> 00:04:16.269
he’s lost touch with his own identity – like
Dr Branhattan.

00:04:16.269 --> 00:04:19.340
So from Meera’s point of view, all this
sacrifice feels empty.

00:04:19.340 --> 00:04:24.410
Their story’s so full of loss and tragedy
– hopefully somehow Bran’s powers will

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:26.139
be worth it.

00:04:26.139 --> 00:04:29.440
Meera leaves to return to her family down
in the Neck.

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:33.449
Meera’s father is Howland Reed, the only
living survivor of the fight at the Tower

00:04:33.449 --> 00:04:36.520
of Joy, where Jon was born to Lyanna Stark.

00:04:36.520 --> 00:04:41.090
So Howland, in the books at least, may play
a role in telling Jon who his parents are

00:04:41.090 --> 00:04:44.740
– he may even be part of a northern conspiracy.

00:04:44.740 --> 00:04:50.699
Also, in the books, it’s likely that Bran
eats Jojen – so go watch that video.

00:04:50.699 --> 00:04:55.729
Arya Stark arrives at Winterfell, her home,
which she hasn’t seen for six seasons.

00:04:55.729 --> 00:05:00.070
She has trouble getting past some guards,
just like she once did in Season 1, but she

00:05:00.070 --> 00:05:02.500
soon reunites with her sister Sansa.

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:08.470
Arya and Sansa had a difficult relationship
as kids – Sansa was proper and ladylike,

00:05:08.470 --> 00:05:13.250
while Arya was an unpredictable tomboy . But
now they’ve grown beyond their childish

00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:14.250
fights.

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:17.560
After all that they’ve been through, all
that they’ve lost, their remaining family

00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:18.970
means everything.

00:05:18.970 --> 00:05:23.850
Arya meets Bran, and like Sansa, she’s a
bit weirded out by the whole psychic robot

00:05:23.850 --> 00:05:25.560
thing Bran’s got going.

00:05:25.560 --> 00:05:30.150
He mentions Arya’s list of people she wants
to kill, and most are dead already.

00:05:30.150 --> 00:05:33.090
Still remaining are Cersei and the Mountain.

00:05:33.090 --> 00:05:38.050
Also Arya thinks the Hound is dead, but he’s
not – maybe they’ll meet again.

00:05:38.050 --> 00:05:41.699
The Starks discuss the dagger, and Arya’s
suspicious about the whole thing.

00:05:41.699 --> 00:05:46.300
It’s looking really likely that the Starks
will find out about Petyr’s deception.

00:05:46.300 --> 00:05:50.760
Bran gives the dagger to Arya, which will
be useful cause Valyrian steel kills white

00:05:50.760 --> 00:05:51.760
walkers.

00:05:51.760 --> 00:05:56.070
Half the main characters on the show have
Valyrian steel now – Jon, Arya, Brienne,

00:05:56.070 --> 00:05:57.699
Jaime – even Sam has one.

00:05:57.699 --> 00:06:01.760
These are the people who’ll kill white walkers
when shit gets real.

00:06:01.760 --> 00:06:04.020
We also get a moment with Brienne.

00:06:04.020 --> 00:06:07.580
For the last few seasons, Brienne’s been
trying to keep her oath to Catelyn Stark to

00:06:07.580 --> 00:06:11.000
find and protect Cat’s daughters Sansa and
Arya.

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:16.100
For most of the story, Brienne wasn’t successful
– she got side-tracked by Stannis and Riverrun,

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:17.930
and the Hound and a bear.

00:06:17.930 --> 00:06:23.150
But now, finally, Catelyn’s daughters are
home – Brienne kept her oath.

00:06:23.150 --> 00:06:27.479
Earlier in the show, Cat called Brienne a
lady, and Brienne said that she’s “no

00:06:27.479 --> 00:06:32.091
lady” . In the books, Pod calls Brienne
ser, but Brienne also isn’t a knight . As

00:06:32.091 --> 00:06:37.780
a female warrior in a patriarchal world, Brienne
has struggled to work out her identity . But

00:06:37.780 --> 00:06:43.039
here Pod calls Brienne my lady, and she starts
to correct him but then just says thanks.

00:06:43.039 --> 00:06:48.060
With her quest complete, Brienne has finally
worked out who she is and so has Pod.

00:06:48.060 --> 00:06:52.400
Lady Brienne may not be a knight, but she
keeps her oaths.

00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:54.110
Brienne later spars with Arya.

00:06:54.110 --> 00:06:58.729
Arya saw Brienne beat the Hound in Season
4, so she wants to have a go at the Maid of

00:06:58.729 --> 00:06:59.729
Tarth.

00:06:59.729 --> 00:07:03.129
Arya doesn’t really swordfight in the books,
she mostly just uses stealth and stuff.

00:07:03.129 --> 00:07:08.060
But she was trained by Syrio Forel, and in
the show by the Faceless Men – as she says,

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:11.450
“No one” – and it looks like all the
training has paid off.

00:07:11.450 --> 00:07:15.139
She holds her own against Brienne which is
hella impressive – Brienne is one of the

00:07:15.139 --> 00:07:18.160
best warriors in Westeros, certainly the strongest
woman.

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:22.470
So Arya’s up there with the best of them
– and now she and Brienne have a mutual

00:07:22.470 --> 00:07:23.470
respect.

00:07:23.470 --> 00:07:28.449
They’ve both felt like outsiders as female
fighters, so this relationship means a lot.

00:07:28.449 --> 00:07:32.140
Sansa watches from above, like Ned once did
in Season 1.

00:07:32.140 --> 00:07:37.169
You can see Sansa realising like, ‘wow okay,
Arya really is a ninja assassin’.

00:07:37.169 --> 00:07:38.970
Just like Bran is a psychic wizard.

00:07:38.970 --> 00:07:42.379
While Sansa’s only special power is fiscal
responsibility.

00:07:42.379 --> 00:07:45.920
Littlefinger’s up there too, and Arya gives
him a menacing glare.

00:07:45.920 --> 00:07:51.150
If Petyr had a half a brain he would run back
to the Vale, like, now.

00:07:51.150 --> 00:07:55.039
Down at Dragonstone, Missandei and Dany talk
about boys, then they head into the caves

00:07:55.039 --> 00:07:56.460
with King Jon.

00:07:56.460 --> 00:07:59.780
Dany leaves her guards behind, which is a
sign she’s starting to trust him.

00:07:59.780 --> 00:08:03.190
The caves are important because they’re
full of dragonglass, which can kill white

00:08:03.190 --> 00:08:04.190
walkers.

00:08:04.190 --> 00:08:08.470
But the caves also contain markings by the
children of the forest, who lived in Westeros

00:08:08.470 --> 00:08:10.849
thousands of years before human beings.

00:08:10.849 --> 00:08:15.500
The markings feature patterns like this spiral
that we’ve seen white walkers make out of

00:08:15.500 --> 00:08:16.500
corpses.

00:08:16.500 --> 00:08:20.430
This makes sense, because the same spiral
pattern appeared at the ritual when the children

00:08:20.430 --> 00:08:25.789
of the forest created the walkers – it looks
like the walkers are imitating the symbols

00:08:25.789 --> 00:08:27.139
of their creators.

00:08:27.139 --> 00:08:31.580
There’s also this circle with a line through
it which has also been made by the walkers,

00:08:31.580 --> 00:08:34.600
and also appears elsewhere in the series.

00:08:34.600 --> 00:08:38.680
This kind of resembles some symbols from George
Martin’s fruity old sci fi stories – if

00:08:38.680 --> 00:08:42.210
you wanna go down the rabbithole of what that
might mean, strap on your tinfoil hat and

00:08:42.210 --> 00:08:47.430
check out this video by Preston Jacobs . It’s
pretty loopy, but is fascinating.

00:08:47.430 --> 00:08:51.500
Jon points out markings showing the children
and the humans fighting together against the

00:08:51.500 --> 00:08:52.500
white walkers.

00:08:52.500 --> 00:08:57.250
Of course, the children originally created
the white walkers as a way to fight humans,

00:08:57.250 --> 00:08:58.860
but Jon’s point still stands.

00:08:58.860 --> 00:09:01.560
People need to come together to fight the
walkers.

00:09:01.560 --> 00:09:05.080
And Jon and Dany are starting to look like
they’d like to come together.

00:09:05.080 --> 00:09:07.900
We know what happened last time Jon was in
a cave with a woman.

00:09:07.900 --> 00:09:11.390
But Dany says she won’t join Jon until he
kneels.

00:09:11.390 --> 00:09:14.770
She says survival is more important than his
pride.

00:09:14.770 --> 00:09:19.730
This is something Jon said to Mance Rayder
in Season 5, but now Jon is in Mance’s position.

00:09:19.730 --> 00:09:23.650
If he kneels, he would lose the respect of
the people who follow him – and then there’d

00:09:23.650 --> 00:09:29.070
be no point in kneeling . Maybe Jon’ll find
some other way to win Dany over.

00:09:29.070 --> 00:09:33.540
On the beach, Dany finds out that the Lannisters
have the reach, so she’s now lost all of

00:09:33.540 --> 00:09:37.030
her allies – the Tyrells, Greyjoys and Dorne.

00:09:37.030 --> 00:09:41.560
Maybe that convoluted plan of taking Casterly
Rock, ferrying Dornish and besieging the capital

00:09:41.560 --> 00:09:43.580
was a bad idea after all.

00:09:43.580 --> 00:09:47.780
Dany suggests just taking throne directly
with her dragons, and again we’re told that

00:09:47.780 --> 00:09:49.530
would kill too many people.

00:09:49.530 --> 00:09:52.020
Which again, might not be strictly true.

00:09:52.020 --> 00:09:56.350
When Dany’s ancestor Aegon took Westeros,
his sister Visenya took the Eyrie by flying

00:09:56.350 --> 00:09:57.970
up there on her dragon.

00:09:57.970 --> 00:10:01.750
She didn’t fight anyone, or burn anything,
she just flew right up and said do you want

00:10:01.750 --> 00:10:05.180
to surrender or do you want my dragon to eat
you – and she won.

00:10:05.180 --> 00:10:08.830
Why can’t Dany fly to the Red Keep and try
something similar?

00:10:08.830 --> 00:10:12.530
It would be risky, and she might have to kill
some people, but isn’t that better than

00:10:12.530 --> 00:10:14.840
killing thousands of soldiers?

00:10:14.840 --> 00:10:18.680
So this whole tension in Dany’s strategy
is questionable.

00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:22.330
But the point the show’s trying to make
is that Dany is willing to do things the hard

00:10:22.330 --> 00:10:24.470
way if it’s the right way.

00:10:24.470 --> 00:10:28.640
Later, Jon and Davos chat with Missandei,
about how Jon is bastard, and Missandei’s

00:10:28.640 --> 00:10:29.640
an ex-slave.

00:10:29.640 --> 00:10:33.180
A lot of Dany and Jon’s people are underdogs.

00:10:33.180 --> 00:10:34.840
Eunuchs, dwarfs, smugglers.

00:10:34.840 --> 00:10:39.170
People who rose from nothing, and united behind
leaders they believe in.

00:10:39.170 --> 00:10:43.360
Theon arrives at Dragonstone, and Jon threatens
to kill him.

00:10:43.360 --> 00:10:46.130
Because in Season 2, Theon betrayed Jon’s
family.

00:10:46.130 --> 00:10:49.960
When Robb sent him to make alliance with the
Greyjoys, Theon stabbed Robb in the back by

00:10:49.960 --> 00:10:52.970
attacking Winterfell, and killing Stark men.

00:10:52.970 --> 00:10:57.090
Jon lets Theon live because he did help Sansa
escape the Boltons – but no one’s letting

00:10:57.090 --> 00:10:59.670
Theon forget his crimes.

00:10:59.670 --> 00:11:03.750
In the books they call him Theon Turncloak
, and just about everyone wants him dead – but

00:11:03.750 --> 00:11:08.750
the gods are not yet done with Theon Greyjoy
. His plan in the show is to rescue his sister

00:11:08.750 --> 00:11:13.670
Yara from Euron – hopefully Euron doesn’t
treat his prisoners as badly as he does in

00:11:13.670 --> 00:11:14.980
the books.

00:11:14.980 --> 00:11:18.690
Somewhere in the south, the Lannisters finish
delivering gold to the capital, when they’re

00:11:18.690 --> 00:11:22.990
attacked by Daenerys with her Dothraki, and
her dragon, Drogon.

00:11:22.990 --> 00:11:27.650
People have been speculating for years how
Dothraki would go on a Westerosi battlefield.

00:11:27.650 --> 00:11:31.600
And most people agree that if you’re safe
in a castle, the Dothraki can’t do much.

00:11:31.600 --> 00:11:36.290
But out in an open field, where they can run
you down, firing arrows from horseback, the

00:11:36.290 --> 00:11:41.300
Dothraki are near unstoppable . This is also
the first time in years that a dragon has

00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:43.310
been used in battle in Westeros.

00:11:43.310 --> 00:11:47.340
Notice at one point how Drogon is shot with
arrows, but they bounce right off his scales

00:11:47.340 --> 00:11:52.070
– younger dragons can be killed with arrows,
but as a dragon grows older, its hide grows

00:11:52.070 --> 00:11:56.680
tougher . Not tough enough, though, to stop
a scorpion bolt.

00:11:56.680 --> 00:12:00.470
Just as Bronn takes a long bow shot to set
off the wildfire at the Blackwater, Bronn

00:12:00.470 --> 00:12:04.940
uses Qyburn’s scorpion to hit Drogon in
the shoulder, wounding him and bringing him

00:12:04.940 --> 00:12:06.200
to ground.

00:12:06.200 --> 00:12:08.760
If that had hit his eye, Drogon might be dead.

00:12:08.760 --> 00:12:13.390
But he burns the scorpion, and faces off against
Jaime, who decides to go jousting against

00:12:13.390 --> 00:12:14.890
a hundred tonne dragon.

00:12:14.890 --> 00:12:19.180
Jaime, remember, killed the Mad King Aerys
– Daenerys’ father.

00:12:19.180 --> 00:12:23.880
If he killed Dany as well, that’d make him
a Queenslayer as well as a Kingslayer.

00:12:23.880 --> 00:12:27.430
He doesn’t succeed though – Bronn knocks
him into water just as he’s about to get

00:12:27.430 --> 00:12:31.100
roasted, kinda like how Tyrion gets knocked
into water last season.

00:12:31.100 --> 00:12:35.740
Bronn made a comment earlier about Jaime’s
riches weighing him down , and now Jaime’s

00:12:35.740 --> 00:12:38.760
rich armour literally weighs him down into
the water.

00:12:38.760 --> 00:12:42.670
Though he most probably will survive.

00:12:42.670 --> 00:12:45.480
The dynamic between Jaime and Tyrion is interesting
here.

00:12:45.480 --> 00:12:50.290
These are both likeable main characters, on
opposite sides of the battle.

00:12:50.290 --> 00:12:54.960
In Book 1, Tyrion tells Catelyn that he never
bets against his family , he’s always on

00:12:54.960 --> 00:12:56.250
team Lannister.

00:12:56.250 --> 00:13:00.800
But here is with Daenerys, as she destroys
his family’s army, and tries to kill his

00:13:00.800 --> 00:13:02.030
brother Jaime.

00:13:02.030 --> 00:13:04.550
Jaime, who rescued Tyrion from prison.

00:13:04.550 --> 00:13:10.260
Jaime, the only one in their family who ever
loved Tyrion . Tyrion is loyal to Dany, but

00:13:10.260 --> 00:13:12.770
he’s also loyal to his brother.

00:13:12.770 --> 00:13:16.040
This tension might be a problem later on.

00:13:16.040 --> 00:13:18.820
Another theme of this scene is the horror
of war.

00:13:18.820 --> 00:13:22.610
Dickon talks about the shock and the smell
of first battle, and there are lots of moments

00:13:22.610 --> 00:13:25.480
of characters gazing at burning men.

00:13:25.480 --> 00:13:30.890
The books spend a lot of time describing the
evils of war, and the impact of war on ordinary

00:13:30.890 --> 00:13:31.890
people.

00:13:31.890 --> 00:13:34.850
The show doesn’t have time for this sort
of slow rumination but it’s able to make

00:13:34.850 --> 00:13:39.160
some of the same points in a really powerful
visual way.

00:13:39.160 --> 00:13:43.990
And that, maybe, is when show is at its best.

00:13:43.990 --> 00:13:44.990
Thanks for watching.

